 this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine"],"id":"long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.16 (Irrationality from divisible coefficient blocks)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.16, p. 49, label thm:weighted-coeff-engine","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $b\\ge2$ be an integer and let $c:\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb N$ satisfy $c(n)\\le n$ for every $n$. Suppose that for every integer $q\\ge1$ there are nonnegative integers $N,K,L,C$, with $K\\le L$, such that\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n b^r&\\mid c(N+r) &&(1\\le r\\le K),\\\\\n \\sum_{r=K+1}^{L}c(N+r)b^{L-r}&\\le C,\\\\\n c(N+L+1+t)&>0 &&\\text{for some integer }t\\ge0,\\\\\n q(C+N+L+2)&<b^L.\n \\end{aligned}\n$$\nThen $\\sum_{n\\ge1}c(n)b^{-n}$ is irrational.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_coeff_series_of_weighted_coeff_block_certificates%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-weighted-coeff-engine%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_coeff_series_of_weighted_coeff_block_certificates%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_coeff_series_of_weighted_coeff_block_certificates"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019